WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Making a Schedule of Loss can take time.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.000
You need to check contracts, payslips and other case files.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
With Lylo, you add the case files and Lylo starts to build the draft.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.300
It pulls out key facts

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.500
and adds the losses into one clear Schedule of Loss.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.000
Open Citations to see where each key figure came from, down to the file and page.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Calculations shows how each total was worked out, so you can check the maths.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.800
If Lylo is not sure about something, it tells you.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:46.000
It marks it for review, so you can check it and make the final call.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.700
You can edit the draft yourself, just like a normal document.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:58.000
Or, tell Lylo what you want changed in chat, and Lylo can update it for you.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.500
You can also add more types of loss, like notice pay, holiday pay, benefits and interest.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:11.800
In the end, you get one clear draft with the facts, maths and points to check all in one place.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.558
Lylo. Less time building. More time on the case.
